.policy "next-practice-server-action-without-auth" revision 1
.description "A Server Action that writes to the database checks the session itself: every exported action is a public POST endpoint, and the page's or middleware's auth check does not cover it."
.language typescript
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.ts", "**/*.mts", "**/*.cts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.js", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.mjs", "**/*.cjs"
.scope exclude "**/*.test.*", "**/*.spec.*", "**/*.cy.*", "**/__tests__/**", "**/test/**", "**/tests/**", "**/e2e/**", "**/__mocks__/**", "**/*.stories.*", "**/*.story.*", "**/__stories__/**", "**/__fixtures__/**", "**/fixtures/**", "**/node_modules/**", "**/dist/**", "**/build/**", "**/out/**", "**/.next/**", "**/coverage/**", "**/vendor/**", "**/.venv/**", "**/.yarn/**", "**/generated/**", "**/__generated__/**", "**/*.generated.*", "**/*.gen.*", "**/*.min.js", "**/*.d.ts"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. Next.js turns every function a 'use server' file exports, and every function with
// its own 'use server' directive, into an endpoint anyone can call with a direct POST request, whatever page shows
// the form. The page's or layout's auth check does not run for that request, and a middleware (proxy) matcher can
// leave the action's path out. So an action that writes rows must find out who is calling inside itself. Outside
// test code, a Server Action is:
//   - a function a top-level 'use server' file exports: `export async function f`, `export const f = async () =>`,
//     or a top-level function listed in `export { f }`;
//   - an exported `const f = w.schema(s).action(async (…) => …)` or `const f = w(schema, async (…) => …)` there: an
//     action built by an action client or wrapper w that resolves to a workspace declaration (next-safe-action,
//     zsa, a home-made `action()`), whose own code is then followed too;
//   - a function whose body starts with 'use server' (an inline action in a Server Component).
// It writes when it, or a workspace function or declaration it calls (by name, through imports tsx/names resolves,
// any depth), makes a Prisma write (`<client>.<model>.create|createMany|createManyAndReturn|update|updateMany|
// updateManyAndReturn|upsert|delete|deleteMany({ where | data | create | update … })`, `$executeRaw`,
// `$executeRawUnsafe`) or a Drizzle one (`db.insert(t).values(…)`, `db.update(t).set(…)`, `db.delete(t).where(…)`).
// It checks the caller when it, or a function it reaches, calls something whose name reads as an auth or session
// check, on camelCase word boundaries (auth, requireAuth, getServerSession, getSession, currentUser, getUser,
// requireUser, validateRequest, requireRole, checkPermission, assertCanEdit, isAdmin, …; never `getAuthor`,
// `OAuth`, `createWorkoutSession` or `updatePermissions`, and never a name whose first word is a write such as
// create, update, delete, set or setup), reads a cookie (`(await cookies()).get("session")`; not cookies().set()),
// reads an `authorization` or `cookie` header (`h.get("authorization")`), or passes headers() on
// (`getSession({ headers: await headers() })`); a headers() read of another header (`x-forwarded-for`) is no check.
// A function the action passes by name to a call (`.use(throwIfSignedIn)`) is followed like one it calls. One
// finding per action, at its name, naming one write.
//   actions.ts:   'use server'
//                 export async function deleteProject(id) {        reported: writes, checks nobody
//                   await prisma.project.delete({ where: { id } }) }
//   actions.ts:   export async function archive(id) {             reported (Via): the write is in a DAL function
//                   await archiveProject(id) }                       it imports (`@/server/projects`, a barrel)
//   actions.ts:   export const leave = actionClient.action(…)      reported (Wrapped): neither the action nor the
//                                                                    client's code checks a session
//   page.tsx:     async function save(fd) { 'use server'; …create } reported: an inline action
//   actions.ts:   const user = await requireUser(); …delete         not reported: checks the session first
//   actions.ts:   calls a helper that calls auth()                   not reported: the check is one call away
//   actions.ts:   memberClient.action(…), memberClient's .use() calls auth()   not reported: the client checks
//   actions.ts:   authActionClient.action(…), protectedAction(…)    not reported: the client's name says it checks
//   actions.ts:   w.action(async ({ ctx }) => …)                     not reported: ctx comes from a middleware
//   actions.ts:   createSafeActionClient().action(…), a package's wrapper   not reported: its code is not read
//   actions.ts:   only reads (findMany) or only revalidatePath()     not reported: no write
//   actions.ts:   signUp, login, resetPassword, subscribe, contact form…   not reported: public by design (a whole
//                 word of the name or of a path folder: `(public)/`, `signup/`, `contact-us/`; `public` only as a
//                 name's first word, `publicAction`)
//   actions.ts:   .use(throwIfSignedIn).action(…) where throwIfSignedIn reads the session   not reported
//   lib/data.ts:  the same functions without 'use server'           not reported: not an endpoint
// Gaps: writes through other clients (Supabase, Mongoose, raw pg), service objects (`svc.remove()`), callbacks
// stored and run later, or packages the resolver cannot find (monorepo workspaces by package name); auth checks by
// any name the pattern misses; an action gated by a secret token it looks up (an emailed link) is reported unless
// its name or folder says it is public. Whether the check's result is used, and whether it checks the right owner
// (authorisation, not only authentication), is not seen: an action that calls auth() and ignores it passes. Imports
// are resolved by tsx/names (the phase tsx_names): relative paths and tsconfig `paths` aliases (`@/`), with the
// extensions and index files TypeScript tries; an ESM `./x.js` specifier for an `x.ts` source is not followed. The
// call graph meets across files at symbols ("src/server/projects#archiveProject"), so two inline actions with the
// same name and text in one file are one. The engine keeps .ts and .tsx files apart, so a call from one into the
// other is not followed: a .tsx action is missed when its write is in a .ts module, and is reported if only a .ts
// helper with a neutral name checks the session.

#include "tsx/names.rerail"

.violation ServerActionWithoutAuth(at: node, x: symbol, what: symbol, p: symbol, o: node)
    "`{x}` is a Server Action, which anyone can call with a direct POST request, and it writes to the database (`{what}` at {p}:{o.line}) without checking who is calling: nothing it runs reads the session or calls an auth check. Verify the user, and that they may change this row, inside the action (e.g. `const session = await auth(); if (!session) throw new Error(\"Unauthorized\")`); the page's, layout's or middleware's check does not run for the action. If `{x}` is a helper that only other server code calls after its own check, move it out of the 'use server' file instead: every export of that file is an endpoint. If the action is public by design (sign-up, a contact form, a token-checked link) or a check this rule cannot see covers it, leave it."
ServerActionWithoutAuth(n, x, what, p, o) :- nsaw_report(f, n, x), !nsaw_wrap(f, _), nsaw_key(f, a), !nsaw_guarded(a),
    nsaw_first_write(f, o), nsaw_write(o, what), docof(o, d), doc(d, p, _).
.violation ServerActionWithoutAuthVia(at: node, x: symbol, g: symbol, what: symbol, p: symbol, o: node)
    "`{x}` is a Server Action, which anyone can call with a direct POST request, and it writes to the database through `{g}()` (`{what}` at {p}:{o.line}) without checking who is calling: nothing it runs reads the session or calls an auth check. Verify the user, and that they may change this row, inside the action before calling `{g}()` (e.g. `const session = await auth(); if (!session) throw new Error(\"Unauthorized\")`); the page's, layout's or middleware's check does not run for the action. If `{x}` is a helper that only other server code calls after its own check, move it out of the 'use server' file instead: every export of that file is an endpoint. If the action is public by design (sign-up, a contact form, a token-checked link) or a check this rule cannot see covers it, leave it."
ServerActionWithoutAuthVia(n, x, gx, what, p, o) :- nsaw_report(f, n, x), !nsaw_wrap(f, _), nsaw_key(f, a),
    !nsaw_guarded(a), !nsaw_first_write(f, _), nsaw_writer(a, k), nsaw_key(g, k), nsaw_first_write(g, o),
    nsaw_fn_name(g, gx), nsaw_write(o, what), docof(o, d), doc(d, p, _).
.violation ServerActionWithoutAuthWrapped(at: node, x: symbol, w: symbol, what: symbol, p: symbol, o: node)
    "`{x}` is a Server Action built with `{w}`, which anyone can call with a direct POST request, and it writes to the database (`{what}` at {p}:{o.line}) without checking who is calling: neither the action nor what `{w}` runs reads the session or calls an auth check. Build it with an action client whose middleware checks the session (a `.use()` step that calls `auth()`, throws when there is no session and passes the user on in `ctx`), or verify the user inside the action; the page's, layout's or middleware's check does not run for the action. If the action is public by design (sign-up, a contact form, a token-checked link) or a check this rule cannot see covers it, leave it."
// The root w resolves to a workspace declaration, in any file, so what it runs can be read. The write named is the
// action's own first, else nsaw_writer's.
ServerActionWithoutAuthWrapped(n, x, w, what, p, o) :- nsaw_report(f, n, x), nsaw_wrap(f, w), docof(f, df),
    nsaw_name_sym(df, w, q), nsaw_unit_key(q), nsaw_key(f, a), !nsaw_guarded(a), nsaw_first_write(f, o),
    nsaw_write(o, what), docof(o, d), doc(d, p, _).
ServerActionWithoutAuthWrapped(n, x, w, what, p, o) :- nsaw_report(f, n, x), nsaw_wrap(f, w), docof(f, df),
    nsaw_name_sym(df, w, q), nsaw_unit_key(q), nsaw_key(f, a), !nsaw_guarded(a), !nsaw_first_write(f, _),
    nsaw_writer(a, k), nsaw_key(g, k), nsaw_first_write(g, o), nsaw_write(o, what), docof(o, d), doc(d, p, _).

// nsaw_report(f, n, x): f is a Server Action named x, reported at n, in a package that uses Next.js, outside tests
// and not public by its name or file path.
.decl nsaw_report(f: node, n: node, x: symbol)
nsaw_report(f, n, x) :- nsaw_action(f, n, x), docof(f, d), nsaw_next_doc(d), !nsaw_test_doc(d),
    !nsaw_public_name(f, x), !nsaw_public_doc(d).
// nsaw_next_doc(d): document d is Next.js code: it imports `next` or a `next/…` module (`next/cache`,
// `next/headers`), or the nearest package.json above it lists next (dependencies, devDependencies or
// peerDependencies). 'use server' is React's, not only Next.js's: a React Router or Waku app has it too.
.decl nsaw_next_doc(d: number)
nsaw_next_doc(d) :- doc(d, p, _), package_for(p, dir), nsaw_next_pkg(dir).
nsaw_next_doc(d) :- nsaw_import(d, _, s, _), (s = "next" ; prefix("next/", s)).
.decl nsaw_next_pkg(dir: symbol)
nsaw_next_pkg(dir) :- package_field(dir, k, _),
    (k = "dependencies/next" ; k = "devDependencies/next" ; k = "peerDependencies/next").
// nsaw_public_name(f, s): unit f's name, export name or value's root name s says it is for signed-out visitors: one
// of the words below as a whole camelCase or snake_case word (`signUp`, `handleSignUp`, `sign_up_user`,
// `unsubscribe`; not `catalogInfo`, `signups`). `public` counts only as the first word (`publicAction`, not
// `makeProjectPublic`). Keyed by the unit, so each file tests its own names.
.decl nsaw_named(f: node, s: symbol)
nsaw_named(f, s) :- nsaw_fn_name(f, s) ; nsaw_vroot(f, s) ; nsaw_exported(f, _, s).
.decl nsaw_public_name(f: node, s: symbol)
nsaw_public_name(f, s) :- nsaw_named(f, s),
    match("(?<pre>.*?)(?<w>(?i:sign_?in|sign_?up|log_?in|register|registration|forgot_?password|forgot|reset_?password|password_?reset|confirm_?email|contact_?(?:form|us)|(?:send|submit)_?contact|(?:un)?subscribe|newsletter|wait_?list|magic_?link|(?:send|verify|check|resend)_?otp|captcha|cookie_?banner))(?<post>.*)", s),
    (pre = "" ; suffix("_", pre) ; match(".*[a-z0-9]", pre), match("[A-Z].*", w)),
    (post = "" ; match("[A-Z0-9_].*", post)).
nsaw_public_name(f, s) :- nsaw_named(f, s), match("public([A-Z0-9_].*)?", s).
// nsaw_public_doc(d): document d's path has a folder or file name that is one of those words, whole
// (`(auth)/signup/`, `contact-us/`, `forgot-password.ts`; not `contacts/`, `verify-domain/`), or a folder named public
// (`(public)/`, `public/`).
.decl nsaw_public_doc(d: number)
nsaw_public_doc(d) :- doc(d, s, _),
    match("(?i)(?:.*[/(_.-])?(?:sign_?-?in|sign_?-?up|log_?-?in|register|registration|forgot_?-?password|forgot|reset_?-?password|password_?-?reset|confirm_?-?email|contact_?-?(?:form|us)|(?:send|submit)_?-?contact|(?:un)?subscribe|newsletter|wait_?-?list|magic_?-?link|(?:send|verify|check|resend)_?-?otp|captcha|cookie_?-?banner)(?:[-_/).].*)?", s).
nsaw_public_doc(d) :- doc(d, s, _), match("(?i)(.*/)?\\(?public\\)?/.*", s).
.decl nsaw_test_doc(d: number)
nsaw_test_doc(d) :- doc(d, p, _),
    match("(?i)(.*/)?(__tests__|tests?|e2e|__mocks__|__fixtures__|fixtures|cypress|playwright)/.*|.*\\.(test|spec|cy|stories|story)\\.[cm]?[jt]sx?", p).

// ---- Server Actions --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// nsaw_action(f, n, x): f is a Server Action named x, or a wrapped one (nsaw_wrap) whose root is yet to resolve; n is
// its name node.
.decl nsaw_action(f: node, n: node, x: symbol)
nsaw_action(f, n, x) :- nsaw_use_server_doc(p), nsaw_exported(f, p, x), nsaw_top(f, p, _, _), nsaw_name_node(f, n).
nsaw_action(f, n, x) :- nsaw_inline(f), nsaw_name_node(f, n), nsaw_fn_name(f, x).
nsaw_action(v, n, x) :- nsaw_wrap(v, _), nsaw_topvar(v, _, x, _), field(v, "name", n).
// nsaw_wrap(v, w): `export const x = w…(async (…) => …)` in a 'use server' file: an action built by a wrapper or
// action client (next-safe-action, zsa, a home-made `action(schema, fn)`) rooted at the name w. It is an action when
// w resolves to a workspace declaration, so what it runs can be read: asked across files where it is reported
// (ServerActionWithoutAuthWrapped). Left out: a root whose name reads as an auth check (`authActionClient`,
// `protectedAction`), a function that takes `ctx` (a client's middleware hands it the user), and a root the resolver
// cannot find (a package, a monorepo workspace).
.decl nsaw_wrap(v: node, w: symbol)
nsaw_wrap(v, w) :- nsaw_use_server_doc(p), nsaw_exported(v, p, _), nsaw_topvar(v, p, _, _),
    field(v, "value", c), kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, f, _), nsaw_fn_value(f),
    !nsaw_ctx(f), nsaw_vroot(v, w), !nsaw_auth_name(v), !nsaw_public_name(v, w).
.decl nsaw_ctx(f: node)
nsaw_ctx(f) :- nsaw_fn_value(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), within(i, ps), text(i, "ctx"),
    (kind(i, "identifier") ; kind(i, "shorthand_property_identifier_pattern") ; kind(i, "property_identifier")).
// nsaw_use_server_doc(p): program p starts with the directive 'use server' (comments and other directives aside).
.decl nsaw_use_server_doc(p: node)
nsaw_use_server_doc(p) :- kind(p, "program"), nsaw_directive(p, p).
// nsaw_inline(f): f's body starts with 'use server'.
.decl nsaw_inline(f: node)
nsaw_inline(f) :- kind(f, k), nsaw_fnk(k), field(f, "body", b), kind(b, "statement_block"), nsaw_directive(b, f).
.decl nsaw_directive(b: node, s: node)
nsaw_directive(b, s) :- (kind(b, "program"), s = b ; kind(b, "statement_block"), field(s, "body", b)), child(b, st, i),
    nsaw_dir_stmt(st, "use server"), count : { child(b, o, j), j < i, !kind(o, "comment"), !nsaw_dir_stmt(o, _) } = 0.
.decl nsaw_dir_stmt(st: node, v: symbol)
nsaw_dir_stmt(st, v) :- kind(st, "expression_statement"), child(st, l, 0), kind(l, "string"), str(l, v).

// ---- functions and their names ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.decl nsaw_fnk(k: symbol)
nsaw_fnk("function_declaration"). nsaw_fnk("function_expression"). nsaw_fnk("function"). nsaw_fnk("arrow_function").
nsaw_fnk("method_definition"). nsaw_fnk("generator_function_declaration").
// nsaw_stmt(p, s, ex): s is a top-level statement of program p, in an export statement when ex = 1.
.decl nsaw_stmt(p: node, s: node, ex: number)
nsaw_stmt(p, s, 0) :- kind(p, "program"), child(p, s, _), !kind(s, "export_statement").
nsaw_stmt(p, s, 1) :- kind(p, "program"), child(p, e, _), kind(e, "export_statement"), field(e, "declaration", s).
// nsaw_top(f, p, x, ex): f is a function program p declares at its top level under the name x:
// `function x() {}` or `const x = async () => {}` (or a function expression).
.decl nsaw_top(f: node, p: node, x: symbol, ex: number)
nsaw_top(f, p, x, ex) :- nsaw_stmt(p, f, ex), kind(f, "function_declaration"), field(f, "name", n), text(n, x).
nsaw_top(f, p, x, ex) :- nsaw_stmt(p, s, ex), (kind(s, "lexical_declaration") ; kind(s, "variable_declaration")),
    child(s, v, _), kind(v, "variable_declarator"), field(v, "name", n), kind(n, "identifier"), text(n, x),
    field(v, "value", f), nsaw_fn_value(f).
.decl nsaw_fn_value(f: node)
nsaw_fn_value(f) :- (kind(f, "arrow_function") ; kind(f, "function_expression") ; kind(f, "function")).
// nsaw_topvar(v, p, x, ex): v is a top-level `const x = …` of program p whose value is not a function: an action
// client, a wrapped action, `const getUser = cache(async () => …)`. Its declarator is a unit of its own.
.decl nsaw_topvar(v: node, p: node, x: symbol, ex: number)
nsaw_topvar(v, p, x, ex) :- nsaw_stmt(p, s, ex), (kind(s, "lexical_declaration") ; kind(s, "variable_declaration")),
    child(s, v, _), kind(v, "variable_declarator"), field(v, "name", n), kind(n, "identifier"), text(n, x),
    field(v, "value", e), !nsaw_fn_value(e).
.decl nsaw_decl(f: node, p: node, x: symbol, ex: number)
nsaw_decl(f, p, x, ex) :- nsaw_top(f, p, x, ex).
nsaw_decl(v, p, x, ex) :- nsaw_topvar(v, p, x, ex).
// nsaw_exported(f, p, y): program p exports its top-level declaration f as y: in its declaration, or by
// `export { x as y }` with no source.
.decl nsaw_exported(f: node, p: node, y: symbol)
nsaw_exported(f, p, x) :- nsaw_decl(f, p, x, 1).
nsaw_exported(f, p, y) :- nsaw_decl(f, p, x, 0), nsaw_listed(p, x, y).
nsaw_exported(f, p, "default") :- kind(p, "program"), child(p, e, _), kind(e, "export_statement"),
    field(e, "declaration", f), kind(f, "function_declaration"), op(e, "default").
// nsaw_vroot(v, w): the value of top-level declarator v is a chain `w.a(…).b(…)` or `w(…)` rooted at the name w.
.decl nsaw_vroot(v: node, w: symbol)
nsaw_vroot(v, w) :- nsaw_topvar(v, _, _, _), field(v, "value", e), nsaw_root(e, w).
.decl nsaw_root_q(e: node)
nsaw_root_q(e) :- nsaw_topvar(v, _, _, _), field(v, "value", e).
nsaw_root_q(g) :- nsaw_root_q(e), (kind(e, "call_expression"), field(e, "function", g) ;
    kind(e, "member_expression"), field(e, "object", g) ; kind(e, "await_expression"), child(e, g, 0)).
.decl nsaw_root(e: node, w: symbol)
nsaw_root(e, w) :- nsaw_root_q(e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, w).
nsaw_root(e, w) :- nsaw_root_q(e), kind(e, "call_expression"), field(e, "function", g), nsaw_root(g, w).
nsaw_root(e, w) :- nsaw_root_q(e), kind(e, "member_expression"), field(e, "object", g), nsaw_root(g, w).
nsaw_root(e, w) :- nsaw_root_q(e), kind(e, "await_expression"), child(e, g, 0), nsaw_root(g, w).
.decl nsaw_listed(p: node, x: symbol, y: symbol)
nsaw_listed(p, x, y) :- kind(p, "program"), child(p, e, _), kind(e, "export_statement"), !field(e, "source", _),
    child(e, c, _), kind(c, "export_clause"), child(c, sp, _), kind(sp, "export_specifier"), field(sp, "name", n),
    text(n, x), (field(sp, "alias", a), text(a, y) ; !field(sp, "alias", _), y = x).
// nsaw_name_node(f, n) and nsaw_fn_name(f, x): a function's own name, or the name of the variable it is assigned to.
.decl nsaw_name_node(f: node, n: node)
nsaw_name_node(f, n) :- kind(f, k), nsaw_fnk(k), field(f, "name", n).
nsaw_name_node(f, n) :- nsaw_fn_value(f), !field(f, "name", _), kind(v, "variable_declarator"), field(v, "value", f),
    field(v, "name", n).
nsaw_name_node(f, f) :- nsaw_inline(f), !field(f, "name", _), count : { field(v, "value", f), kind(v, "variable_declarator") } = 0.
nsaw_name_node(v, n) :- nsaw_topvar(v, _, _, _), field(v, "name", n).
.decl nsaw_fn_name(f: node, x: symbol)
nsaw_fn_name(f, x) :- nsaw_name_node(f, n), n != f, text(n, x).
nsaw_fn_name(f, "(inline action)") :- nsaw_name_node(f, f).

// ---- what an action runs ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The call graph crosses files by symbol alone (decision 0677): each file's rules give its units keys and say which
// symbols each runs (nsaw_edge, nsaw_pass); only the closure over those keys (nsaw_reach) joins files, and the
// findings relate it back to the action's and the write's nodes.
// nsaw_unit(f): a function the call graph follows: a top-level function or declaration, or an inline action.
.decl nsaw_unit(f: node)
nsaw_unit(f) :- nsaw_top(f, _, _, _).
nsaw_unit(v) :- nsaw_topvar(v, _, _, _).
nsaw_unit(f) :- nsaw_inline(f).
// nsaw_in(c, f): call c is in unit f, in callbacks inside it too (`prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => …)`).
.decl nsaw_in(c: node, f: node)
nsaw_in(c, f) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), inside(c, f, nsaw_fnk), nsaw_unit(f).
nsaw_in(c, v) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), inside(c, v, "variable_declarator"), nsaw_topvar(v, _, _, _).
// nsaw_key(g, k): unit g's key. A top-level declaration's is its symbol, "module#name", the one an import of it from
// another file resolves to (nsaw_name_sym). An inline action nested in a function has none: its key is its module,
// its name and a hash of its text.
.decl nsaw_key(g: node, k: symbol)
nsaw_key(g, @qname(m, x)) :- nsaw_decl(g, p, x, _), docof(p, d), ts_module(d, m).
nsaw_key(f, @qname(m, cat(x, "@", @sha256(s)))) :- nsaw_inline(f), !nsaw_top(f, _, _, _), nsaw_fn_name(f, x),
    text(f, s), docof(f, d), ts_module(d, m).
// nsaw_alias(k, j): a unit exported under another name (`export { f as g }`, `export default function f`) is also
// that name's symbol k; j is its key.
.decl nsaw_alias(k: symbol, j: symbol)
nsaw_alias(@qname(m, y), j) :- nsaw_exported(g, p, y), nsaw_decl(g, p, x, _), y != x, nsaw_key(g, j), docof(p, d),
    ts_module(d, m).
// nsaw_unit_key(k): k names a unit, by its key or an exported name.
.decl nsaw_unit_key(k: symbol)
nsaw_unit_key(k) :- nsaw_key(_, k).
nsaw_unit_key(k) :- nsaw_alias(k, _).
// nsaw_fn_key(k): k names a top-level function, by its key or an exported name.
.decl nsaw_fn_key(k: symbol)
nsaw_fn_key(k) :- nsaw_top(h, _, _, _), nsaw_key(h, k).
nsaw_fn_key(@qname(m, y)) :- nsaw_top(h, p, x, _), nsaw_exported(h, p, y), y != x, docof(p, d), ts_module(d, m).
// nsaw_edge(k, q): the unit keyed k runs the unit named q: a call in it resolves to q (nsaw_callee_sym), its value is
// a chain rooted at the name of q (`actionClient.use(…)`), or k is an exported name of q.
.decl nsaw_edge(k: symbol, q: symbol)
nsaw_edge(k, q) :- nsaw_in(c, g), nsaw_key(g, k), nsaw_callee_sym(c, q).
nsaw_edge(k, q) :- nsaw_vroot(g, w), nsaw_key(g, k), docof(g, d), nsaw_name_sym(d, w, q).
nsaw_edge(k, q) :- nsaw_alias(k, q).
// nsaw_pass(k, q): the unit keyed k passes the name of q to a call (`.use(throwIfSignedIn)`, `items.map(removeItem)`):
// what it hands over is run, when q is a function.
.decl nsaw_pass(k: symbol, q: symbol)
nsaw_pass(k, q) :- nsaw_in(c, g), nsaw_key(g, k), field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, a, _), kind(a, "identifier"),
    text(a, x), docof(c, d), nsaw_name_sym(d, x, q).
// nsaw_root_key(a): a reported action's key.
.decl nsaw_root_key(a: symbol)
nsaw_root_key(a) :- nsaw_report(f, _, _), nsaw_key(f, a).
// nsaw_reach(a, k): the action keyed a runs the unit named k: itself, one a call it reaches resolves to, or a
// function it passes by name to a call. Across files, by symbol.
.decl nsaw_reach(a: symbol, k: symbol) cross_file
nsaw_reach(a, a) :- nsaw_root_key(a).
nsaw_reach(a, q) :- nsaw_reach(a, k), nsaw_edge(k, q).
nsaw_reach(a, q) :- nsaw_reach(a, k), nsaw_pass(k, q), nsaw_fn_key(q).
// nsaw_first_write(g, o): o is unit g's first write.
.decl nsaw_first_write(g: node, o: node)
nsaw_first_write(g, o) :- nsaw_unit(g), o = min y : { nsaw_in(y, g), nsaw_write(y, _) }.
// nsaw_writer(a, k): the unit the action keyed a reaches whose write a finding names: of those it reaches that
// write, the one whose key is least.
.decl nsaw_writes(a: symbol, k: symbol)
nsaw_writes(a, k) :- nsaw_reach(a, k), nsaw_writing(k).
.decl nsaw_writes_before(a: symbol, k: symbol)
nsaw_writes_before(a, k) :- nsaw_writes(a, k), nsaw_writes(a, j), j < k.
.decl nsaw_writer(a: symbol, k: symbol)
nsaw_writer(a, k) :- nsaw_writes(a, k), !nsaw_writes_before(a, k).
// nsaw_writing(k): the unit keyed k writes.
.decl nsaw_writing(k: symbol)
nsaw_writing(k) :- nsaw_key(g, k), nsaw_first_write(g, _).
// nsaw_checks(k): the unit keyed k makes an auth or session check.
.decl nsaw_checks(k: symbol)
nsaw_checks(k) :- nsaw_key(g, k), nsaw_in(c, g), nsaw_auth_call(c).
// nsaw_guarded(a): the action keyed a reaches an auth or session check.
.decl nsaw_guarded(a: symbol)
nsaw_guarded(a) :- nsaw_reach(a, k), nsaw_checks(k).

// nsaw_write(c, what): c writes rows. Prisma: `a.model.m({ … })` with a write method m and an object literal
// argument holding where, data, create or update (so `url.searchParams.delete("x")` and `map.delete(k)` are
// not writes); `a.$executeRaw…`. Drizzle: `a.insert(t).values(…)`, `a.update(t).set(…)`, `a.delete(t).where(…)`.
.decl nsaw_write(c: node, what: symbol)
nsaw_write(c, cat(mx, ".", m, "()")) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", fn),
    kind(fn, "member_expression"), field(fn, "property", pr), text(pr, m), nsaw_write_method(m),
    field(fn, "object", mo), kind(mo, "member_expression"), field(mo, "property", mp), text(mp, mx),
    match("[a-zA-Z]\\w*", mx), field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, a, 0), kind(a, "object"), nsaw_prisma_arg(a).
nsaw_write(c, cat(m, "()")) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", fn), kind(fn, "member_expression"),
    field(fn, "property", pr), text(pr, m), (m = "$executeRaw" ; m = "$executeRawUnsafe").
nsaw_write(c, cat(m, "(…).", s, "()")) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", fn),
    kind(fn, "member_expression"), field(fn, "property", sp), text(sp, s), field(fn, "object", i),
    kind(i, "call_expression"), field(i, "function", ifn), kind(ifn, "member_expression"), field(ifn, "property", ip),
    text(ip, m), (m = "insert", s = "values" ; m = "update", s = "set" ; m = "delete", s = "where"),
    field(i, "arguments", al), child(al, t, 0), (kind(t, "identifier") ; kind(t, "member_expression")).
.decl nsaw_write_method(m: symbol)
nsaw_write_method("create"). nsaw_write_method("createMany"). nsaw_write_method("createManyAndReturn").
nsaw_write_method("update"). nsaw_write_method("updateMany"). nsaw_write_method("updateManyAndReturn").
nsaw_write_method("upsert"). nsaw_write_method("delete"). nsaw_write_method("deleteMany").
.decl nsaw_prisma_arg(a: node)
nsaw_prisma_arg(a) :- kind(a, "object"), child(a, pr, _), (kind(pr, "pair"), field(pr, "key", k), text(k, x) ;
    kind(pr, "shorthand_property_identifier"), text(pr, x)), (x = "where" ; x = "data" ; x = "create" ; x = "update").

// nsaw_auth_call(c): c reads the session or checks the caller: its callee's name (`auth()`, `getSession()`,
// `supabase.auth.getUser()`, `auth.api.getSession()`) reads as one, it reads a cookie (`(await cookies()).get(…)`,
// `store.get(…)` for `const store = await cookies()`; a cookies().set() is no check), it reads an authorization,
// cookie or API-key header (`(await headers()).get("authorization")`, `req.headers.get("cookie")`), or it is a
// headers() call passed on to another call (`getSession({ headers: await headers() })`). headers() alone is no
// check: actions read it for the client's IP or locale. The receiver's name is not read: `session.save()` and
// `auth.update()` are no checks.
.decl nsaw_auth_call(c: node)
nsaw_auth_call(c) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", fn), nsaw_auth_name(fn).
nsaw_auth_call(c) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", fn), kind(fn, "member_expression"),
    field(fn, "property", pr), text(pr, "get"), field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, a, 0), str(a, s),
    match("(?i)authorization|cookie|x-api-key|api-key", s).
nsaw_auth_call(c) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", fn), nsaw_callee_name(fn, "headers"),
    (e = c ; kind(e, "await_expression"), child(e, c, 0)),
    (child(al, e, _), kind(al, "arguments") ;
     kind(pr, "pair"), field(pr, "value", e), child(o, pr, _), kind(o, "object"), child(al, o, _), kind(al, "arguments")).
// nsaw_auth_call(c) for a cookie read: `.get(…)`, `.getAll()` or `.has(…)` on cookies() (awaited or not), or on a
// name the same function binds to it.
nsaw_auth_call(c) :- nsaw_cookie_read(c, o), nsaw_cookies_value(o).
nsaw_auth_call(c) :- nsaw_cookie_read(c, o), kind(o, "identifier"), text(o, x), nearest(o, f, nsaw_fnk),
    nsaw_cookie_var(f, x).
// nsaw_cookie_read(c, o): c is `o.get(…)`, `o.getAll()` or `o.has(…)`.
.decl nsaw_cookie_read(c: node, o: node)
nsaw_cookie_read(c, o) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", fn), kind(fn, "member_expression"),
    field(fn, "property", pr), text(pr, m), (m = "get" ; m = "getAll" ; m = "has"), field(fn, "object", o).
// nsaw_cookie_var(f, x): function f binds x to cookies() (`const store = await cookies()`).
.decl nsaw_cookie_var(f: node, x: symbol)
nsaw_cookie_var(f, x) :- nsaw_cookies_value(e), field(v, "value", e), kind(v, "variable_declarator"), field(v, "name", n),
    text(n, x), nearest(v, f, nsaw_fnk).
// nsaw_cookies_value(e): e is `cookies()`, `await cookies()`, or either in parentheses.
.decl nsaw_cookies_value(e: node)
nsaw_cookies_value(e) :- kind(e, "call_expression"), field(e, "function", fn), kind(fn, "identifier"), text(fn, "cookies").
nsaw_cookies_value(e) :- (kind(e, "await_expression") ; kind(e, "parenthesized_expression")), child(e, g, 0),
    nsaw_cookies_value(g).
.decl nsaw_callee_name(fn: node, x: symbol)
nsaw_callee_name(fn, x) :- kind(fn, "identifier"), text(fn, x).
nsaw_callee_name(fn, x) :- kind(fn, "member_expression"), field(fn, "property", pr), text(pr, x).
// nsaw_auth_name(n): callee n's name, or the root name of top-level declarator n's value (a wrapper), reads as an
// auth check, matched on camelCase word boundaries (keyed by the node, so each file tests its own names):
//   - the word Auth (Authed, Authenticated, Authorize…) anywhere, unless the first word is a write (create, update,
//     delete, set, setup, enable, remove, …: `setupTwoFactorAuth`, `removeAuthToken`); never Author or OAuth;
//   - a read verb, then Session or User (`getServerSession`, `getKindeServerSession`, `requireUserId`,
//     `currentUser`, `getSessionOrThrow`), not `createWorkoutSession`, `getSessionBySlug` or `getUserById`;
//   - a check verb, then Role, Permission, Access, Admin, Member or Owner (`requireRole`, `checkHasAccess`,
//     `isAdmin`), or `assertCan…`; not `updatePermissions`;
//   - a few fixed names: validateRequest, verifyToken, jwtVerify, protect, authGuard, isLoggedIn, viewer…
// A workspace helper with another name is still followed into, so its own auth() call counts. Gaps: a package's
// helper under another name (`getRequiredUser`, `serverUser`, `getToken`, `getCurrentAdmin`, `verifyOwnership`).
// These names are a naming convention, not an API: a check under a name none of them reads as is missed.
.decl nsaw_auth_name(n: node)
nsaw_auth_name(n) :- nsaw_name_q(n, x), match("((.*[a-z0-9])?Auth|(.*_)?auth)(enticat[a-z]*|oriz[a-z]*|ed|s)?([A-Z0-9_].*)?", x),
    !match("(create|update|delete|remove|set|add|insert|upsert|save|reset|enable|disable|setup|start|end|send|resend|initiate|complete|generate|handle|to|revoke|clear|sign|log|register|refresh|store|persist|mark|link|unlink|connect|disconnect|invite)([A-Z0-9_].*)?", x).
nsaw_auth_name(n) :- nsaw_name_q(n, x),
    (match("(get|require|validate|verify|check|ensure|assert|use|read|load|fetch)(Server|Iron|Auth|User|Current|Active|Valid|Supabase|Kinde|Optional)*Session(Or[A-Z0-9][A-Za-z0-9]*|User|Token|Cookie|Data|From[A-Z][A-Za-z]*)?|session(User|Or[A-Z][A-Za-z]*)?", x) ;
     match("(get|require|ensure|assert|check|validate|verify|use|fetch|load|read|current)(Server|Current|Authenticated|Auth|Session|Signed|Logged|In|Valid|Optional|Active)*User(Id|Or[A-Z0-9][A-Za-z0-9]*|Session|From[A-Z][A-Za-z]*)?", x) ;
     match("(require|check|assert|ensure|verify|validate|has|is|can)([A-Z][a-z0-9]*)*(Role|Roles|Permission|Permissions|Access|Admin|Member|Membership|Owner|Scope|Scopes)(OrThrow|OrRedirect|For[A-Z][A-Za-z]*|In[A-Z][A-Za-z]*|On[A-Z][A-Za-z]*)?|(assert|check|ensure|require)Can[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*", x) ;
     match("(?i)(current_?user|get_?me|whoami|validate_?request|verify_?(token|jwt|access_?token|id_?token|session_?cookie|api_?key|request)|jwt_?verify|protect(ed[a-z_]*)?|(auth|role|admin|access|route|session|user|api|login)_?guard|guard|with_?(auth_?)?guard|(is|require|check|ensure)_?(logged|signed)_?in|signed_?in|logged_?in|require_?login|(get|require|current)_?viewer|viewer|current_?member|(require|ensure)_?(org|organization|workspace|team|user)|ensure_?user)", x)).
.decl nsaw_name_q(n: node, x: symbol)
nsaw_name_q(n, x) :- nsaw_callee_name(n, x) ; nsaw_vroot(n, x).

// ---- call targets, by symbol -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// nsaw_callee_sym(c, q): call c runs the unit named q: `x()` for a name x that nsaw_name_sym resolves; `ns.y()` for
// `import * as ns from "s"`, s's export y.
.decl nsaw_callee_sym(c: node, q: symbol)
nsaw_callee_sym(c, q) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", fn), kind(fn, "identifier"), text(fn, x),
    docof(c, d), nsaw_name_sym(d, x, q).
nsaw_callee_sym(c, q) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", fn), kind(fn, "member_expression"),
    field(fn, "object", o), kind(o, "identifier"), text(o, ns), field(fn, "property", pr), text(pr, y), docof(c, d),
    nsaw_import(d, ns, s, "*"), target(d, s, t), (tsx_names__exports(t, y, q) ; q = @qname(t, y)).
// nsaw_name_sym(d, x, q): the name x, in document d, names the symbol q: a top-level declaration of d (when no import
// binds x), "module#x"; or the export an import of x names (`import { y as x } from "s"`, `import x from "s"`), as
// tsx/names resolves it (target: relative paths and tsconfig `paths`) and follows it through `export { x as y } from
// "s"` and `export * from "s"` (barrels: tsx_names__exports). "s#y" too, which an `export default function f` of s
// is known by (nsaw_alias).
.decl nsaw_name_sym(d: number, x: symbol, q: symbol)
nsaw_name_sym(d, x, q) :- nsaw_import(d, x, s, y), y != "*", target(d, s, t),
    (tsx_names__exports(t, y, q) ; q = @qname(t, y)).
nsaw_name_sym(d, x, @qname(m, x)) :- nsaw_decl(_, p, x, _), docof(p, d), ts_module(d, m), !nsaw_import(d, x, _, _).
// nsaw_import(d, x, s, y): document d binds local name x to export y of module s ("default", "*" or a name).
// `import type` binds no value.
.decl nsaw_import(d: number, x: symbol, s: symbol, y: symbol)
nsaw_import(d, x, s, y) :- kind(sp, "import_specifier"), nearest(sp, i, "import_statement"), !op(i, "type"),
    field(i, "source", sn), str(sn, s), docof(i, d), field(sp, "name", n), text(n, y),
    (field(sp, "alias", a), text(a, x) ; !field(sp, "alias", _), x = y).
nsaw_import(d, x, s, "default") :- kind(cl, "import_clause"), child(cl, id, 0), kind(id, "identifier"), text(id, x),
    nearest(cl, i, "import_statement"), !op(i, "type"), field(i, "source", sn), str(sn, s), docof(i, d).
nsaw_import(d, x, s, "*") :- kind(ns, "namespace_import"), child(ns, id, 0), text(id, x),
    nearest(ns, i, "import_statement"), field(i, "source", sn), str(sn, s), docof(i, d).

